  "facts": [
    "The Goethals Bridge, named after Major General George Washington Goethals, opened its new eastbound span on June 10, 2017, replacing a 1928 cantilever bridge that had served the area for 89 years.",
    "Designed as a single‑span cable‑stayed structure, each new bridge features a 900‑foot main span, 12‑foot lanes, and a 10‑foot pedestrian and bicycle walkway added to the westbound span in 2018.",
    "The 2018 replacement earned ENR New York’s Project of the Year award, recognizing its engineering excellence, safety innovations, and the seamless transition of traffic during the demolition of the old cantilever bridge."
